    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0332" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg312"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extracts.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Pike to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 129.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">The Hague,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 5th instant, No. 146.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>The London conference on the Dano-German question will have great difficulties to
                    overcome, as you are aware, but it is presumed that it can hardly fail <pb
                        facs="0333" n="313" xml:id="pg313"/> to restore peace. A favorite plan of
                    settlement seems to be the union of the north half of Schleswig with Denmark as
                    an integral part of the kingdom; the remainder to go with Holstein into the
                    German Confederation, under the King of Denmark as its duke.</p>
                <p>Our new minister of foreign affairs, Mr. Cremers, is thus far very successful in
                    his office, though never before in public life.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES S. PIKE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
